  "goodToKnow": "Der Wirkstoff is an active ingredient in a medicine or pesticide: Der Wirkstoff heißt Paracetamol. German package leaflets (Beipackzettel) list it first. At Bayer in 1897, chemist Felix Hoffmann synthesised acetylsalicylic acid, sold as Aspirin from 1899. Wirken means to have an effect: Das Mittel wirkt schnell. Die Wirkung is effect, and die Nebenwirkung a side effect. Plural: die Wirkstoffe."
